hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"0","Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi informed us, Abdullah ibn al-Rumi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit, from Anas, that Fatimah wept for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and she said: ""O my father, from his Lord, how near he is! O my father, to Gabriel he is mourned! O my father, Paradise of Firdaws is his abode!"""",""2 : 499"",""And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was brought something from the dates of charity. I took a date and put it in my mouth, and he took it with his saliva until he returned it to the dates. It was said to him: ""O Messenger of Allah, what was upon you from this date from this child?"" He said: ""We, the family of Muhammad, charity is not lawful for us."""",12 : 196,""""I heard the Messenger of Allah [SAW] say: ""The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the Muhajir is the one who forsakes (Hajara) that which Allah has forbidden to him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4996)"",""12 : 252"",""And I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: ""Whoever wears silk, it will be forbidden for him to wear it in the Hereafter."""",""12 : 253"",""Abu Ya'la informed us, said: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Dawud al-Sarraj, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and if he enters Paradise, the people of Paradise will wear it, but he will not wear it."""",12 : 254,""Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Whoever has (the following) four characteristics will be a pure hypocrite: ""If he speaks, he tells a lie; if he gives a promise, he breaks it, if he makes a covenant he proves treacherous; and if he quarrels, he behaves in a very imprudent evil insulting manner (unjust). And whoever has one of these characteristics, has one characteristic of a hypocrite, unless he gives it us."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3178)"",""12 : 255"",""Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Sinan informed us, said: Ahmad ibn Abi Bakr informed us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saw a silk garment at the door of the mosque, so he said: ""O Messenger of Allah, if only you would buy this and wear it on Friday and for delegations when they come to you."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears this."" Then silk garments came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he gave Umar ibn al-Khattab one of them. Umar said: ""O Messenger of Allah, you clothed me with it, yet you said about the silk garment of Utarid what you said."" The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I did not clothe you with it to wear it."" So Umar gave it to a brother of his who was a polytheist in Mecca."",12 : 325,""The Prophet ﷺ as saying: The two months of 'Id (festival), Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah, are not defective. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2323)"",""12 : 326"",""Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa Abdan informed us, said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, said: Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: ""When you hear the barking of dogs or the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge with Allah, for they see what you do not see. And reduce going out when the feet have settled, for Allah, Glorified and Exalted, disperses from His creation in His night whatever He wills. And close the doors and mention the name of Allah upon them, for Satan does not open a door that has been closed and had the name of Allah mentioned upon it. And cover the vessels, and invert the containers, and tie the water skins."" Abu Ya'la informed us, said: Al-Qawariri narrated to us, said: Yazid ibn Zuri' narrated to us, said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated similarly."",12 : 327,""There is no god but Allah; there is a destruction in store for Arabia because of the turmoil which is near at hand as the barrier of Gog and Magog has been opened like it, and he (in order to explain it) made a ring with the help of his thumb and forefinger. I said: Messenger of Allah, would we be destroyed despite the fact that there would be pious people amongst us? He said: Yes, when evil would be predominant. (Using translation from Muslim 2880c)"",""12 : 328"",""Abu Ya'la informed us, said: Abu Kurayb narrated to us, said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A house burned in Medina with its people at night. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was informed about their situation, he said: ""This fire is your enemy, so when you sleep, extinguish it from yourselves."""",""12 : 329"",""Abu Khalifah informed us, said: Musaddad ibn Musarhad narrated to us, said: Khalid ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand, and something afflicts him, let him blame no one but himself."""",""12 : 330"",""Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb al-Balkhi informed us, said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, said: Abu al-Ahwas informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Al-Bara', may Allah be pleased with him, said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, took to his bed, he would place his right hand under his right cheek, then say: ""O Allah, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants."""",13 : 110,""The Muslim who offends most against the Muslims is he who enquires about something which has not been forbidden to men, and it is declared forbidden because of his enquiry. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4610)"",""13 : 182"",""Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani informed us, Abu al-Tahir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, said: I heard Al-Thawri narrating, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever plays with dice (nard), it is as if he dipped his hand in the flesh and blood of a pig."""",""13 : 183"",""Abu Ya'la informed us, said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salam al-Jumahi narrated to us, said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, saw a man following a pigeon, so he said: ""A devil following a female devil."" Abu Hatim said: ""The one who plays with pigeons, his play does not go beyond pursuing them with what Allah, Glorified and Exalted, dislikes. And the one who commits what Allah dislikes is a sinner, and the sinner may be called a devil, even if he is from the children of Adam. Allah the Exalted said: 'Devils of humans and jinn' [6:112], so He named the sinners among them devils. And the Prophet's, peace and blessings be upon him, calling the pigeon a devil is due to proximity, and because the action of the sinner in playing with it extended to it."""",13 : 185,""If this verse were revealed in relation to the Jews (i e. ""This day I have perfected your religion for you and have completed My favours for you and have chosen for you al-Islam as religion"") we would have taken the day of rejoicing on which this verse was revealed. Thereupon 'Umar said: I know the day on which it was revealed and the hour when it was revealed and where Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been when it was revealed. It was revealed on the night of Friday and we were in 'Arafat with Messenger of Allah ﷺ at that time. (Using translation from Muslim 3017b)"",13 : 186,""“The adulterer, at the time he is committing adultery, is not a believer; (the wine drinker) at the time he is drinking, is not a believer; the thief, at the time he is stealing, is not a believer; the plunderer, at the time he is plundering with the people looking on, is not a believer.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3936)"",13 : 480,The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: By his good character a believer will attain the degree of one who prays during the night and fasts during the day. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4798),""13 : 481"",""Abu Ya'la informed us, said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, said: Yahya ibn Atiq narrated to me, from Ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no contagion, and no bad omens, and I like good omens."""",""13 : 482"",""Al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us, said: Harmalah narrated to us, said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, said: Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""There is no contagion."""",""13 : 54"",""Al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dhuhli narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, from Iyad ibn Abdullah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, went out on Eid al-Adha or Eid al-Fitr to the prayer ground, prayed, then turned and stood, admonished the people and ordered them to give charity. He said: ""O people, give charity."" Then he turned and passed by the women and said: ""O women, give charity, for I see you are the majority of the people of Hell."" They said: ""Why is that, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""You curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands. I have not seen anyone from those deficient in intellect and religion more able to take away the mind of a prudent man than one of you, O women."" They said to him: ""What is the deficiency of our religion and intellect, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Is not the testimony of a woman equal to half the testimony of a man?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""That is the deficiency of her intellect. Is it not that when a woman menstruates, she does not pray and does not fast?"" They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""That is the deficiency of her religion."""",14 : 311,""“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood (in prayer) until his feet became swollen. It was said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, Allah has forgiven you your past and future sins.’ He said: ‘Should I not be a thankful slave?’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1419)"",""14 : 497"",""Al-Fadl ibn al-Hubab informed us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qurrah ibn Khalid, Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir narrated to us, saying: We were at al-Mirbad when I saw a disheveled man holding a piece of leather. We said to him: ""You appear to be a man from the people of the desert?"" He said: ""Yes."" We said to him: ""Give us this piece of leather in your hand."" We took it and read what was in it, and it contained: ""From Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, to Banu Zuhayr: Give the fifth of the spoils, and the Prophet's share and the choicest portion, and you are safe under Allah's protection and His Messenger's protection."" We said: ""Who wrote this for you?"" He said: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."""",14 : 516,He who believes in Allah and in the last day should honour his guest; he who believes in Allah and in the last day should not harm his neighbor; he who believes in Allah and in the last day should speak good or keep silence. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5154),""14 : 517"",""Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Al-Fadl ibn Musa informed us, from Yazid ibn Ziyad ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, at the market of Dhu al-Majaz wearing a red suit, and he was saying: ""O people, say 'There is no god but Allah' and you will succeed."" A man was following him throwing stones at him, and his heels and ankles had bled, and he was saying: ""O people, do not obey him, for he is a liar."" I said: ""Who is this?"" It was said: ""This is the slave of Banu Abd al-Muttalib."" I said: ""Then who is this following him throwing stones?"" He said: ""This is Abd al-Uzza Abu Lahab."""",""14 : 585"",""Ibn Qutaybah informed us, Yazid ibn Mawhib narrated to us, Al-Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abbad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr, that Aisha informed him, that she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and listened to him before he died, while his head was resting on her chest, saying: ""O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, and join me with the Highest Companion."""",""14 : 586"",""Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi' informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Assar narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, that Ibn Abbas and Aisha informed him, that when death approached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, he would put a corner of his cloak over his face, and when he felt distressed, he would uncover it, saying: ""May Allah curse the Jews and Christians, they took the graves of their prophets as mosques."" Aisha said: ""He was warning them against doing what they did."""",14 : 587,None of you should make another one stand in the meeting and then occupy his place. (Using translation from Muslim 2177a),""14 : 592"",""Imran ibn Musa ibn Mujashi' informed us, Isma'il ibn Yunus narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, saying: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was overcome by agony, his head was in Fatimah's lap. Fatimah said: ""Oh, the agony of your agony today, O my father!"" He raised his head, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: ""No agony for your father after today, O Fatimah."" When he died, Fatimah said: ""O my father, who answered his Lord's call! O my father, how near he is to his Lord! O my father, to the Garden of Firdaws is his abode! O my father, to Gabriel we announce his death!"" Anas said: When we buried him, I passed by Fatimah's house and she said: ""O Anas, did your souls find it good to throw dust on the Messenger of Allah?"""",""14 : 83"",""Abu Khalifah informed us, saying: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Sakhr ibn Jawriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, descended in the year of Tabuk at al-Hijr near the houses of Thamud. People drew water from the wells that Thamud used to drink from, set up pots, and kneaded flour. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Overturn the pots and feed the dough to the camels."" Then he traveled until he descended at the place where the she-camel used to drink, and said: ""Do not enter upon these people who were punished, lest what afflicted them afflict you."""",14 : 84,""If anyone pursues a path in search of knowledge, Allah will thereby make easy for him a path to paradise; and he who is made slow by his actions will not be speeded by his genealogy. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3643)"",15 : 188,""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer at al-Hudaibiyyah after rain which has fallen during the night, and when he finished, he turned to the people and said: Do you know what your Lord has said ? They said: Allah and His Apostle know best. He said: This morning there were among mt servants one who believes in me and one who disbelieves. The one who said: ""We have been given rain by Allah's grace and mercy"" is the one who believes in me and disbelieves in the star ; but the one who said: ""We have been given rain by such and such a rain star,"" is the one who disbelieves in me and believes in the star. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3906)"",15 : 33,""The commencement of the Divine Inspiration to Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the form of good righteous (true) dreams in his sleep. He never had a dream but that it came true like bright day light. He used to go in seclusion (the cave of) Hira where he used to worship(Allah Alone) continuously for many (days) nights. He used to take with him the journey food for that (stay) and then come back to (his wife) Khadija to take his food like-wise again for another period to stay, till suddenly the Truth descended upon him while he was in the cave of Hira. The angel came to him in it and asked him to read. The Prophet ﷺ replied, ""I do not know how to read."" (The Prophet ﷺ added), ""The angel caught me (forcefully) and pressed me so hard that I could not bear it anymore. He then released me and again asked me to read, and I replied, ""I do not know how to read,"" whereupon he caught me again and pressed me a second time till I could not bear it anymore. He then released me and asked me again to read, but again I replied, ""I do not know how to read (or, what shall I read?)."" Thereupon he caught me for the third time and pressed me and then released me and said, ""Read: In the Name of your Lord, Who has created (all that exists). Has created man from a clot. Read and Your Lord is Most Generous...up to..... ..that which he knew not."" (96.15) Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned with the Inspiration, his neck muscles twitching with terror till he entered upon Khadija and said, ""Cover me! Cover me!"" They covered him till his fear was over and then he said, ""O Khadija, what is wrong with me?"" Then he told her everything that had happened and said, 'I fear that something may happen to me."" Khadija said, 'Never! But have the glad tidings, for by Allah, Allah will never disgrace you as you keep good reactions with your Kith and kin, speak the truth, help the poor and the destitute, serve your guest generously and assist the deserving, calamityafflicted ones."" Khadija then accompanied him to (her cousin) Waraqa bin Naufal bin Asad bin ʿAbdul ʿUzza bin Qusai. Waraqa was the son of her paternal uncle, i.e., her father's brother, who during the Pre-Islamic Period became a Christian and used to write the Arabic writing and used to write of the Gospels in Arabic as much as Allah wished him to write. He was an old man and had lost his eyesight. Khadija said to him, ""O my cousin! Listen to the story of your nephew."" Waraqa asked, ""O my nephew! What have you seen?"" The Prophet ﷺ described whatever he had seen. Waraqa said, ""This is the same Namus (i.e., Gabriel, the Angel who keeps the secrets) whom Allah had sent to Moses. I wish I were young and could live up to the time when your people would turn you out."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, ""Will they turn me out?"" Waraqa replied in the affirmative and said: ""Never did a man come with something similar to what you have brought but was treated with hostility. If I should remain alive till the day when you will be turned out then I would support you strongly."" But after a few days Waraqa died and the Divine Inspiration was also paused for a while and the Prophet ﷺ became so sad as we have heard that he intended several times to throw himself from the tops of high mountains and every time he went up the top of a mountain in order to throw himself down, Gabriel would appear before him and say, ""O Muhammad! You are indeed Messenger of Allah ﷺ in truth"" whereupon his heart would become quiet and he would calm down and would return home. And whenever the period of the coming of the inspiration used to become long, he would do as before, but when he used to reach the top of a mountain, Gabriel would appear before him and say to him what he had said before. (Ibn ʿAbbas said regarding the meaning of: 'He it is that Cleaves the daybreak (from the darkness)' (6.96) that Al-Asbah. means the light of the sun during the day and the light of the moon at night). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6982)"",""15 : 42"",""Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Azdi informed us, saying: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, saying: Al-Walid informed us, saying: Al-Awza'i narrated to me, saying: Al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: There will be caliphs after me who act according to what they know and do what they are commanded. Then there will be caliphs after them who act according to what they do not know and do what they are not commanded. Whoever denounces them is absolved, but whoever is pleased and follows them."",""15 : 43"",""Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Ali ibn al-Ja'd al-Jawhari narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah informed us, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Al-Aswad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani, saying: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saying: There will be twelve caliphs after me, all of them from Quraysh. When he returned home, Quraysh came to him, saying: ""Then what will happen?"" He said: ""Then there will be chaos."""",""Uthman replied"",""""""Whenever a verse was revealed from the Quran"","" the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ  would call someone to write it down and instruct them to place it in the Surah where it should be mentioned. Al-Anfal was revealed in Madinah"","" and Bara'ah was revealed towards the end of the Quran. However"","" the Prophet passed away without informing us where to place it. I found its content similar to the content of Surah Al-Anfal"","" so I combined them together. However"","" I didn't write the phrase 'Bismillah hir-Rahman ir-Rahim' between them"","" so I placed it in the seventh long Surah."""""""",""15 : 87"",""Ahmad ibn Hamdan ibn Musa al-Tustari at Abbadan informed us, saying: Abu Sa'id al-Ashaj narrated to us, saying: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The Euphrates will soon uncover a treasure of gold. Whoever is present should not take anything from it. Ahmad ibn Hamdan narrated it to us again in its aftermath, saying: Abu Sa'id al-Ashaj narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, Abu al-Zinad narrated from Al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, like it except he said: ""It will uncover a mountain of gold."""",16 : 102,""Abu Tufail, come to us. There has been a difference of opinion between me and my friend about the companion of Moses whom he wanted to meet on the way. Did hear anything from Allah's meesenger ﷺ making a mention of anything? Ubayy said: I heard Messenger of Allah (may Peace be upon him) as saying: As Moses was amongst the group of Bani Isra'il, there came to him a person and he said to him: Do you know anyone having better knowledge than you? Moses said: No. Thereupon Allah revealed to Moses: Of course, there is amongst Our servants Khadir (who has better knowledge) than you. Moses asked the way of meeting him. Allah made the fish a sign and it was said to him: Where you miss the fish return to that (place) and you will soon find him. So Moses moved on as Allah wished him to move on. He then said to his young companion: Bring for us the breakfast. Thereupop that young man said to Moses. when he asked him for the breakfast: Don't you see that as we had reached the Sakhra I forgot the fish and nobody made it forget (in our mind) but the satan that I should remind you of it? Mosed said to that young man: This was what we wanted. So they retraced their steps and met Khadir and the events which followed have been described in His Book except that Yunus (the narrator) said that he followed the traces of fish in the ocean. (Using translation from Muslim 2380f)"",""16 : 104"",""Ibn Qutaybah informed us, Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed us, from Ibn Shihab, Urwah informed me, that Aisha said: Doesn't Abu Hurayrah amaze you? He came and sat at the door of my room narrating about the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, making me hear that, while I was glorifying Allah. He left before I finished my glorification. Had I caught up to him, I would have replied to him: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, did not narrate hadith in a continuous manner like your narration."",""16 : 268"",""Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Zahmewayh narrated to us, Ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Shafi' who was a physician, saying: Usayd ibn Hudayr summoned me, so I cut his sciatic nerve. He narrated two hadiths to me. He said: Two families from my people came to me: a family from Banu Zafar and a family from Banu Mu'awiyah. They said: ""Speak to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, to allot for us or give us."" So I spoke to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and he said: ""Yes, I will allot for each family half a share, and if Allah restores to us, we will restore to them."" I said: ""May Allah reward you with good, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""And you, may Allah reward you with good, for I have not known you to be anything but chaste and patient."""",""16 : 276"",""Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Mus'ab ibn Abd Allah ibn Mus'ab al-Zubayri narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qudamah ibn Ibrahim, saying: I saw al-Hajjaj striking Abbas ibn Sahl during Ibn al-Zubayr's governorship. Sahl ibn Sa'd came to him, an old man with two braids, wearing two garments: a waist-wrapper and a cloak. He stood between the two rows and said: ""O Hajjaj, do you not preserve the Messenger of Allah's will concerning us?"" He said: ""What did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, will concerning you?"" He said: ""He willed that good be done to the righteous of the Ansar, and the wrongdoers among them be pardoned."""",""16 : 278"",""Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sami informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Dinar informed me, he heard Ibn Umar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Ghifar: ""May Allah forgive Ghifar, and Aslam, may Allah keep them safe. And Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."""",16 : 279,""""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, we were made up of nine; five and four. The first of the numbers for the Arabs, and the latter for the non-Arabs. He said: 'Listen, have you heard that after me there will leaders, whoever enters upon them and condones to their lies, and supports them in their oppression, then he is not from me and I am not from him, and he shall not drink with me from the Hawd. And whoever does not enter upon them, nor help them in their oppression, nor condones to their lies, then he is from me, and I am from him, and he shall drink with me at the Hawd.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2259)"",16 : 417,""“Whoever claims to belong to someone other than his father, or (a freed slave) who claims that his Wala is for other than his real master, the curse of Allah (SWT), the angels and all the people will be upon him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2609)"",""16 : 418"",""Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Salm informed us, saying: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Darraj narrated to him, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: That the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: And raised couches, and by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, their elevation is like the distance between the heaven and the earth, and the distance between the heaven and the earth is a journey of five hundred years."",16 : 98,""""I took a walk with the Prophet ﷺ on a farm in Al-Madinah, and when he reclined upon a palm-leaf stalk, a group of Jews were passing by. Some of them said, 'We should question him.' Others said: 'Do not question him for he might tell you something that you do not like.' They said to him: 'O Abul-Qasim, narrated to us about the Ruh.' The Prophet ﷺ stood for some time, he raised his head toward the heavens, and I recognized revelation was coming to him, until the revelation ceased. Then he ﷺ said: ""The Ruh is one of the things, the knowledge of which is only with my Lord. And of knowledge, you have been given only a little (17:85).'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3141)"",22,""“What is this noise?” They said: “Palm trees that are being pollinated.” He said: “If they did not do that it would be better.” So they did not pollinate them that year, and the dates did not mature properly. they mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: “If it is one of the matters of your religion, then refer to me.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2471)"",23,""What are you doing? They said: We are grafting them, whereupon he said: It may perhaps be good for you if you do not do that, so they abandoned this practice (and the date-palms) began to yield less fruit. They made a mention of it (to the Holy Prophet), whereupon he said: I am a human being, so when I command you about a thing pertaining to religion, do accept it, and when I command you about a thing out of my personal opinion, keep it in mind that I am a human being. 'Ikrima reported that he said something like this. (Using translation from Muslim 2362)"",29,""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: '""Whoever narrates a Hadith from me thinking it to be false, then he is one of the two liars."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 41)"
"30","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us: “It is sufficient for a man to be considered sinful that he relates everything he hears.”"",31,""‘Whoever lies upon me intentionally, then let him take his seat in the Fire’. (Using translation from Muslim 3)"",33,""The commencement of the Divine Inspiration to Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the form of good righteous (true) dreams in his sleep. He never had a dream but that it came true like bright day light. He used to go in seclusion (the cave of) Hira where he used to worship(Allah Alone) continuously for many (days) nights. He used to take with him the journey food for that (stay) and then come back to (his wife) Khadija to take his food like-wise again for another period to stay, till suddenly the Truth descended upon him while he was in the cave of Hira. The angel came to him in it and asked him to read. The Prophet ﷺ replied, ""I do not know how to read."" (The Prophet ﷺ added), ""The angel caught me (forcefully) and pressed me so hard that I could not bear it anymore. He then released me and again asked me to read, and I replied, ""I do not know how to read,"" whereupon he caught me again and pressed me a second time till I could not bear it anymore. He then released me and asked me again to read, but again I replied, ""I do not know how to read (or, what shall I read?)."" Thereupon he caught me for the third time and pressed me and then released me and said, ""Read: In the Name of your Lord, Who has created (all that exists). Has created man from a clot. Read and Your Lord is Most Generous...up to..... ..that which he knew not."" (96.15) Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned with the Inspiration, his neck muscles twitching with terror till he entered upon Khadija and said, ""Cover me! Cover me!"" They covered him till his fear was over and then he said, ""O Khadija, what is wrong with me?"" Then he told her everything that had happened and said, 'I fear that something may happen to me."" Khadija said, 'Never! But have the glad tidings, for by Allah, Allah will never disgrace you as you keep good reactions with your Kith and kin, speak the truth, help the poor and the destitute, serve your guest generously and assist the deserving, calamityafflicted ones."" Khadija then accompanied him to (her cousin) Waraqa bin Naufal bin Asad bin ʿAbdul ʿUzza bin Qusai. Waraqa was the son of her paternal uncle, i.e., her father's brother, who during the Pre-Islamic Period became a Christian and used to write the Arabic writing and used to write of the Gospels in Arabic as much as Allah wished him to write. He was an old man and had lost his eyesight. Khadija said to him, ""O my cousin! Listen to the story of your nephew."" Waraqa asked, ""O my nephew! What have you seen?"" The Prophet ﷺ described whatever he had seen. Waraqa said, ""This is the same Namus (i.e., Gabriel, the Angel who keeps the secrets) whom Allah had sent to Moses. I wish I were young and could live up to the time when your people would turn you out."" Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, ""Will they turn me out?"" Waraqa replied in the affirmative and said: ""Never did a man come with something similar to what you have brought but was treated with hostility. If I should remain alive till the day when you will be turned out then I would support you strongly."" But after a few days Waraqa died and the Divine Inspiration was also paused for a while and the Prophet ﷺ became so sad as we have heard that he intended several times to throw himself from the tops of high mountains and every time he went up the top of a mountain in order to throw himself down, Gabriel would appear before him and say, ""O Muhammad! You are indeed Messenger of Allah ﷺ in truth"" whereupon his heart would become quiet and he would calm down and would return home. And whenever the period of the coming of the inspiration used to become long, he would do as before, but when he used to reach the top of a mountain, Gabriel would appear before him and say to him what he had said before. (Ibn ʿAbbas said regarding the meaning of: 'He it is that Cleaves the daybreak (from the darkness)' (6.96) that Al-Asbah. means the light of the sun during the day and the light of the moon at night). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6982)"
"34","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I was in retreat in the cave of Hira. When my retreat ended, I descended from the cave and came to the lower part of the valley. Then I was called out to. I looked in front of me, behind me, to my right and to my left, but I saw nothing.” Then I was called again. I looked above me, and there was an angel sitting on a throne between the sky and the earth. I became frightened of him and came to Khadijah. I said: Cover me, cover me, pour cold water over me. Then this verse was revealed to me: “O you who wraps himself [in a cloak], arise and warn, and magnify your Lord.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In the narration from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), it is mentioned that « » was revealed first in the Qur'an, while in the narration from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), it is mentioned that « » was revealed first. There is no contradiction between these two narrations because Allah the Exalted revealed « » to His Messenger when he was in the cave of Hira. Then he returned home, and Sayyidah Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her) covered him with a cloak and poured cold water over him, and in the house of Sayyidah Khadijah (may Allah be pleased with her), « » was revealed to him. So there is no difference or contradiction between these two narrations."
"35","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) about this: so he said: ( « » ) was revealed first. So I said: (Was this revealed first) or Iqra (was revealed first)? He said: I will tell you what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us. He said: “I stayed in seclusion in the cave of Hira for a month. When I completed my seclusion, I came down from the mountain. When I reached the lower part of the valley, I was called by a voice. I looked in front of me, behind me, to my right and to my left, but I saw no one. Then I was called again. I looked towards the sky, and there he (an angel) was, on a throne in the open space. Because of this, I was overcome with intense fear. I came to Khadijah and, at my request, she covered me with a cloak and then poured water over me. Then Allah Almighty revealed to me this verse: ‘O you who are wrapped in a cloak! Arise and warn, and magnify your Lord, and purify your garments.’”"
"36","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then a stealthy listener (a jinn) hears this statement, and sometimes, before he can convey it downwards, a shooting star overtakes him, and sometimes the shooting star does not reach him, so he passes it to the one below him. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) (or perhaps the narrator) said: They are thus positioned one above the other. The narrator named Sufyan demonstrated with his hand how they pass the information to each other, until it reaches the earth and is placed into the mouth of a disbeliever or a sorcerer. He (the devil) mixes a hundred lies with it. Sometimes, the original statement is confirmed (or it turns out to be true), so it is said: 'Did he not say such-and-such on such-and-such a day? He spoke the truth.'"",37,""""When Allah, the exalted, speaks to send revelation, the inhabitants of heaven hear the clanging of a bell from the heavens like a chain being dragged across a rock, and they swoon. They continue to remain like that until Jibril comes to them. When he comes to them, they recover and say: 'O Jibril, what did your Lord say?' He would say: 'The truth,' and they would say: 'The truth, the truth.'"" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4738)"",38,""Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'How does the Revelation come to you?' He said: 'Like the ringing of a bell, and this is the hardest on me. When it departs I remember what he said. And sometimes the Angel appears to me in the form of a man and speaks to me, and I remember what he said."" Aishah said: ""I saw him when the Revelation came to him on a very cold day, and his forhead was dripping with sweat."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 934)"
"39","I demonstrate the movement of those lips as the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, used to move them, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse regarding it. ""Do not move your tongue with it to hasten it. Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation."" Our master Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: By its collection is meant ""to gather it in your chest."" Then you recite this verse: ""We recite it: so follow its recitation."" Our master Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: That is, you listen to it attentively and remain silent. ""Then upon Us is its explanation."" By this is meant, then your recitation of it is upon Us. Our master Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: Then when Gabriel, peace be upon him, would come to the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, would listen to it attentively, and when Gabriel, peace be upon him, would leave, the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, would recite that verse just as Gabriel, peace be upon him, had recited it before him."
"40","Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When this verse was revealed, “The believers who sit (at home) are not equal...” the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bring Zayd to me. He came with a tablet and inkpot (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), or a shoulder blade and inkpot. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Write this: “The believers who sit (at home) and those who strive in the way of Allah are not equal.” The narrator says: At"
"41","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bring me a shoulder blade or a tablet, then he dictated this verse: “The believers who sit ("
"42","narrates: When this verse was revealed: “Those among the believers who sit (at home) are not equal...” the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called Sayyiduna Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him). He came with a shoulder blade (bone) and wrote this verse on it. Sayyiduna Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him) complained about his blindness, so this verse was revealed: “Except those who are afflicted (with disability).”"
"43","I said to Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him): For what reason did you combine Surah Anfal and Surah Tawbah together? Even though Surah Tawbah is a surah of two hundred verses, and Surah Anfal is from the Mathani. You combined both? So Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: Whenever any verse of the Qur’an was revealed, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would call for a scribe, and then he would say to them, “Include these in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned.” So Surah Anfal was also revealed in Madinah Munawwarah, and this surah (Tawbah) was also revealed in Madinah Munawwarah in the last period of revelation. When the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, he did not specify to us where we should place them, so I found that its incident resembled the incident of Surah Anfal. Therefore, I combined both of them, and we did not write the line of “ « » ” between them. I included them among the seven long surahs."",""Uthman replied"",""""""Whenever a verse was revealed from the Quran"","" the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ  would call someone to write it down and instruct them to place it in the Surah where it should be mentioned. Al-Anfal was revealed in Madinah"","" and Bara'ah was revealed towards the end of the Quran. However"","" the Prophet passed away without informing us where to place it. I found its content similar to the content of Surah Al-Anfal"","" so I combined them together. However"","" I didn't write the phrase 'Bismillah hir-Rahman ir-Rahim' between them"","" so I placed it in the seventh long Surah."""""""
"44","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), no one has asked me about this after that. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) had informed that when the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed away, (some time before his passing) revelation was being sent down to him more frequently."
"45","The Qur'an did. He responded: Did the Qur'an? So I recited this verse: ""Glory be to Him Who took His servant by night..."" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) recited it in the same way, up to this verse: ""Indeed, He is the Hearing, the Seeing."" He asked: Do you think that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed there? I replied: No. He said: A beast was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Here, the narrator named Hammad mentioned this, and the narrator named Asim also described its appearance, but I do not remember its appearance. Sayyiduna Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) made the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mount it, and one of the two sat behind the other. So that beast set out with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that very night, until it reached Bayt al-Maqdis. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was shown the things in the heavens and the earth. Then both of them returned, just as they had gone, they returned in the same way. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not pray there. If the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had prayed (there), it would have become a Sunnah."",46,""that Al-Buraq was brought to the Prophet ﷺ on the Night of Isra, saddled and reined, but he shied from him. So Jibra'il said to him: ""is it from Muhammad that you do this? By your Lord! There is no one more honorable to your Lord than him."" He said: ""Then he started sweating profusely."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3131)"
"47","I was taken on the Night Journey, I reached Bayt al-Maqdis. Jibreel (peace be upon him) opened a hole in the large stone with his finger and tied the Buraq to it.”"",48,""Malik bin Sasaa said that Messenger of Allah ﷺ described to them his Night Journey saying, ""While I was lying in Al-Hatim or Al-Hijr, suddenly someone came to me and cut my body open from here to here."" I asked Al-Jarud who was by my side, ""What does he mean?"" He said, ""It means from his throat to his pubic area,"" or said, ""From the top of the chest."" The Prophet ﷺ further said, ""He then took out my heart. Then a gold tray of Belief was brought to me and my heart was washed and was filled (with Belief) and then returned to its original place. Then a white animal which was smaller than a mule and bigger than a donkey was brought to me."" (On this Al-Jarud asked, ""Was it the Buraq, O Abu Hamza?"" I (i.e. Anas) replied in the affirmative). The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The animal's step (was so wide that it) reached the farthest point within the reach of the animal's sight. I was carried on it, and Gabriel set out with me till we reached the nearest heaven. When he asked for the gate to be opened, it was asked, 'Who is it?' Gabriel answered, 'Gabriel.' It was asked, 'Who is accompanying you?' Gabriel replied, 'Muhammad.' It was asked, 'Has Muhammad been called?' Gabriel replied in the affirmative. Then it was said, 'He is welcomed. What an excellent visit his is!' The gate was opened, and when I went over the first heaven, I saw Adam there. Gabriel said (to me). 'This is your father, Adam; pay him your greetings.' So I greeted him and he returned the greeting to me and said, 'You are welcomed, O pious son and pious Prophet.' Then Gabriel ascended with me till we reached the second heaven. Gabriel asked for the gate to be opened. It was asked, 'Who is it?' Gabriel answered, 'Gabriel.' It was asked, 'Who is accompanying you?' Gabriel replied, 'Muhammad.' It was asked, 'Has he been called?' Gabriel answered in the affirmative. Then it was said, 'He is welcomed. What an excellent visit his is!' The gate was opened. When I went over the second heaven, there I saw Yahya (i.e. John) and ʿIsa (i.e. Jesus) who were cousins of each other. Gabriel said (to me), 'These are John and Jesus; pay them your greetings.' So I greeted them and both of them returned my greetings to me and said, 'You are welcomed, O pious brother and pious Prophet.' Then Gabriel ascended with me to the third heaven and asked for its gate to be opened. It was asked, 'Who is it?' Gabriel replied, 'Gabriel.' It was asked, 'Who is accompanying you?' Gabriel replied, 'Muhammad.' It was asked, 'Has he been called?' Gabriel replied in the affirmative. Then it was said, 'He is welcomed, what an excellent visit his is!' The gate was opened, and when I went over the third heaven there I saw Joseph. Gabriel said (to me), 'This is Joseph; pay him your greetings.' So I greeted him and he returned the greeting to me and said, 'You are welcomed, O pious brother and pious Prophet.' Then Gabriel ascended with me to the fourth heaven and asked for its gate to be opened. It was asked, 'Who is it?' Gabriel replied, 'Gabriel' It was asked, 'Who is accompanying you?' Gabriel replied, 'Muhammad.' It was asked, 'Has he been called?' Gabriel replied in the affirmative. Then it was said, 'He is welcomed, what an excel lent visit his is!' The gate was opened, and when I went over the fourth heaven, there I saw Idris. Gabriel said (to me), 'This is Idris; pay him your greetings.' So I greeted him and he returned the greeting to me and said, 'You are welcomed, O pious brother and pious Prophet.' Then Gabriel ascended with me to the fifth heaven and asked for its gate to be opened. It was asked, 'Who is it?' Gabriel replied, 'Gabriel.' It was asked. 'Who is accompanying you?' Gabriel replied, 'Muhammad.' It was asked, 'Has he been called?' Gabriel replied in the affirmative. Then it was said He is welcomed, what an excellent visit his is! So when I went over the fifth heaven, there I saw Harun (i.e. Aaron), Gabriel said, (to me). This is Aaron; pay him your greetings.' I greeted him and he returned the greeting to me and said, 'You are welcomed, O pious brother and pious Prophet.' Then Gabriel ascended with me to the sixth heaven and asked for its gate to be opened. It was asked. 'Who is it?' Gabriel replied, 'Gabriel.' It was asked, 'Who is accompanying you?' Gabriel replied, 'Muhammad.' It was asked, 'Has he been called?' Gabriel replied in the affirmative. It was said, 'He is welcomed. What an excellent visit his is!' When I went (over the sixth heaven), there I saw Moses. Gabriel said (to me),' This is Moses; pay him your greeting. So I greeted him and he returned the greetings to me and said, 'You are welcomed, O pious brother and pious Prophet.' When I left him (i.e. Moses) he wept. Someone asked him, 'What makes you weep?' Moses said, 'I weep because after me there has been sent (as Prophet) a young man whose followers will enter Paradise in greater numbers than my followers.' Then Gabriel ascended with me to the seventh heaven and asked for its gate to be opened. It was asked, 'Who is it?' Gabriel replied, 'Gabriel.' It was asked,' Who is accompanying you?' Gabriel replied, 'Muhammad.' It was asked, 'Has he been called?' Gabriel replied in the affirmative. Then it was said, 'He is welcomed. What an excellent visit his is!' So when I went (over the seventh heaven), there I saw Abraham. Gabriel said (to me), 'This is your father; pay your greetings to him.' So I greeted him and he returned the greetings to me and said, 'You are welcomed, O pious son and pious Prophet.' Then I was made to ascend to Sidrat-ul-Muntaha (i.e. the Lote Tree of the utmost boundary) Behold! Its fruits were like the jars of Hajr (i.e. a place near Medina) and its leaves were as big as the ears of elephants. Gabriel said, 'This is the Lote Tree of the utmost boundary) . Behold ! There ran four rivers, two were hidden and two were visible, I asked, 'What are these two kinds of rivers, O Gabriel?' He replied,' As for the hidden rivers, they are two rivers in Paradise and the visible rivers are the Nile and the Euphrates.' Then Al-Bait-ul-Ma'mur (i.e. the Sacred House) was shown to me and a container full of wine and another full of milk and a third full of honey were brought to me. I took the milk. Gabriel remarked, 'This is the Islamic religion which you and your followers are following.' Then the prayers were enjoined on me: They were fifty prayers a day. When I returned, I passed by Moses who asked (me), 'What have you been ordered to do?' I replied, 'I have been ordered to offer fifty prayers a day.' Moses said, 'Your followers cannot bear fifty prayers a day, and by Allah, I have tested people before you, and I have tried my level best with Bani Israel (in vain). Go back to your Lord and ask for reduction to lessen your followers' burden.' So I went back, and Allah reduced ten prayers for me. Then again I came to Moses, but he repeated the same as he had said before. Then again I went back to Allah and He reduced ten more prayers. When I came back to Moses he said the same, I went back to Allah and He ordered me to observe ten prayers a day. When I came back to Moses, he repeated the same advice, so I went back to Allah and was ordered to observe five prayers a day. When I came back to Moses, he said, 'What have you been ordered?' I replied, 'I have been ordered to observe five prayers a day.' He said, 'Your followers cannot bear five prayers a day, and no doubt, I have got an experience of the people before you, and I have tried my level best with Bani Israel, so go back to your Lord and ask for reduction to lessen your follower's burden.' I said, 'I have requested so much of my Lord that I feel ashamed, but I am satisfied now and surrender to Allah's Order.' When I left, I heard a voice saying, 'I have passed My Order and have lessened the burden of My Worshipers."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 3887)"",49,""""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'On the night on which I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by Musa, peace be upon him, and he was praying in his grave.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1634)"",50,I came. And in the narration transmitted on the authority of Haddib (the words are): I happened to pass by Moses on the occasion of the Night journey near the red mound (and found him) saying his prayer in his grave. (Using translation from Muslim 2375a),51,""that the Prophet ﷺ said: ""When I was taken on the Night of Isra I met Musa."" He described him saying: ""He was a man who was"" and I think he said: ""A thin man, whose hair was as if he was a man from Shanu'ah."" He said: ""I met 'Eisa"" he described him saying: ""Of average build, with a red face, as if he had just come out of the Dimas"" meaning the bath-house. ""And I saw Ibrahim"" he said: ""I am the one among his offspring that most resembles him"" and he said: ""I was brought two vessels, one of them containing milk and the other containing wine. I was told: 'Take whichever one of them you wish.' So I took the milk to drink from it. It was said to me: 'You were guided to the Fitrah' or: 'You chose the Fitrah, if you had take the wine your Ummah would have strayed.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3130)"",52,""Praise is due to Allah Who guided you to the true nature; had you taken the one containing wine, Your Umma would have gone astray. (Using translation from Muslim 168b)"
"53","I was taken on the Mi'raj, I saw some people whose lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I asked: O Jibreel! Who are these people? He replied: These are the preachers of your Ummah who used to enjoin good upon the people but forgot themselves, even though they used to recite the Book. Do they not have sense?"" The Shaykh says: This narration has been transmitted by Abu 'Atab from Hisham, from Mughira, from Malik bin Dinar, from Thumama, from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and he has made a mistake in it, because the narrator Yazid bin Zuray' is more ""meticulous"" than two hundred men like Abu 'Atab."
"54","I entered Paradise, and there was a palace made of gold. I asked: Whose palace is this? The angels replied: It belongs to a man from the Quraysh. I thought perhaps it was mine, so I asked: Whose is it? It was said: It is Umar bin Al-Khattab's."" (Then the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said to Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him:) O Abu Hafs! If I had not considered your sense of honor, I would have entered it. Sayyiduna Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah! I may become angry with anyone, but I can never be angry with you."",55,""that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""When the Quraish belied me, I stood in the Hijr, and Allah displayed Bait Al-Maqdis to me, so I informed them of its features as I was looking at it."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3133)"",56,""Regarding the Statement of Allah"" ""And We granted the vision (Ascension to the heavens) which We made you see (as an actual eye witness) was only made as a trial for the people."" (17.60) Ibn ʿAbbas added: The sights which Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shown on the Night Journey when he was taken to Bait-ulMaqdis (i.e. Jerusalem) were actual sights, (not dreams). And the Cursed Tree (mentioned) in the Qur'an is the tree of Zaqqum (itself) . (Using translation from Bukhārī 3888)"
"57","The words of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace be upon him) saw his Lord,"" mean that the Prophet (peace be upon him) saw his Lord with his heart at such a station where no human being can reach, because that station and rank is very lofty."
"58","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I saw a light. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This means that he did not see his Lord, but rather he saw that light among the created lights, the ""exalted light"" (i.e., the lights that are higher than the rest of creation)."
"59","narration transmitted from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him), which we have already mentioned."
"60","narrations are contradictory, whereas this is not the case. Because Allah Almighty granted His Messenger superiority over all other prophets. To the extent that our master Jibreel (peace be upon him) came so close to his Lord as the distance of two bows, and at that time our master Jibreel (peace be upon him) taught him. At that time, the Prophet (peace be upon him) saw him (or perhaps Allah Almighty) with the eye of the heart, as He willed. The meaning of the narration from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Prophet (peace be upon him) cannot perceive Him, is: You cannot do so in the state of sleep or wakefulness. The statement of Allah Almighty: ""Vision cannot perceive Him"" means: Vision cannot perceive Him; His sight will be on the Day of Resurrection, but when vision sees Him, it will not be able to perceive Him, because perception means to encompass, and sight means to see, and the vision of Allah Almighty is possible, but the reality cannot be comprehended. Because comprehension can be of the creation, and it is possible for the servant to see his Lord. The narration from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that vision cannot perceive Him, means that vision cannot perceive Him in this world or the Hereafter, but among His servants, He can, by His grace, make whomever He wills capable of it. The word ""dunya"" (world) sometimes refers to the earths and the heavens and the space between them, because these things were the beginning. Allah Almighty created them so that good deeds for the Hereafter could be earned in them, which will come after this beginning. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) saw his Lord at a place where the word ""dunya"" does not apply, because at that time he was even closer than the distance of two bows. Therefore, the meaning of the narration from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) will be: The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not see Him in this world. Thus, there is no contradiction or difference between these two narrations."",61,""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""A group of my Ummah will continue to prevail and they will never be harmed by those who forsake them, until the Hour begins."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 6)"
"62","The narrator named Abdullah bin Abdullah Razi is trustworthy, and he is a resident of Kufa."
"63","I am most entitled to that statement among you. And when you hear something attributed to me that your mind rejects, and your hair and skin feel aversion to it, and you feel that you are distant from it, then I am the most distant from that statement among you.”"
"64","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only record the Qur'an from me. Whoever has recorded anything from me other than that, let him erase it."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet Muhammad's (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibition of recording anything other than the Qur'an means: He (peace and blessings be upon him) encouraged the memorization of hadiths, lest people record the hadiths and then not memorize them or reflect upon them. The evidence for the correctness of this position is that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) allowed Sayyiduna Abu Shah Yamani to record the sermon of the Farewell Pilgrimage, which he had heard from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) himself. Similarly, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) also allowed Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) to record hadiths."
"65","The meaning of the words in the narration “we had some knowledge about it” is that regarding the commands, prohibitions, information, actions, and declarations of permissibility by the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), (we had received knowledge)."
"66","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “May Allah keep that person happy who hears something from us and then conveys it exactly as he heard it, because sometimes the one to whom it is conveyed understands it better than the one who heard it directly.”"",67,""“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up in Khaif in Mina, and said: ‘May Allah make his face shine, the man who hears my words and conveys them. It may be that the bearer of knowledge does not understand it, and it may be that he takes it to one who will understand it more than he does. There are three things in which the heart of the believer does not betray: sincerity of action for the sake of Allah, offering sincere advice to the rulers of the Muslims, and adhering to the Jama’ah (main body of the Muslims). Their supplication is answered (i.e. encompassing every good, and all of the people).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3056)"
"68","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah have mercy on the person who hears something from me and then conveys it to others just as he heard it, because sometimes the one to whom it is conveyed preserves it better than the one who heard it directly."",69,""""I heard 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud narrating from his father who said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'May Allah gladden a man who hears something from us, so he conveys it as he heard it. Perhaps the one it is conveyed to is more understanding than the one who heard it.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2657)"
"70","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The keys of the unseen are five. No one except Allah knows what the wombs will bring forth (i.e., whether a boy will be born or a girl will be born), and no one except Allah knows what will happen tomorrow. No one except Allah knows when it will rain. And no person knows on which land he will die. And no person knows when the Hour (Day of Judgment) will be established.”"",71,""Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The keys of Unseen are five which none knows but Allah: None knows what will happen tomorrow but Allah; none knows what is in the wombs (a male child or a female) but Allah; none knows when it will rain but Allah; none knows at what place one will die; none knows when the Hour will be established but Allah."" (See The Qur'an 31:34."") (Using translation from Bukhārī 4697)"
"72","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah Almighty dislikes every harsh-natured, arrogant, miserly person who shouts in the markets, who sleeps at night like a corpse, and spends the day like a donkey. He is knowledgeable about worldly matters, but ignorant about the Hereafter.”"
"73","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the statement of Allah Almighty: ""He it is Who has sent down to you the Book; in it are verses that are clear."
"74","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""The Qur'an has been revealed to me in seven modes.\"" To argue about the Qur'an is disbelief. (He said this three times, then said:) \""Whatever of it you understand, act upon it, and whatever you do not have knowledge of, refer it to one who knows.\"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \""W"
"75","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “The Qur’an has been revealed upon seven letters. Every verse has an apparent meaning and a hidden meaning.” « » Mention of the prohibition that people should not argue about the Book of Allah Almighty, and the command to disassociate from anyone who does so."",76,""""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the following Verse: 'It is He Who has sent down to you (Muhammad) the Book (this Qur'an). In it are verses that are entirely clear, they are the foundations of the Book; and others not entirely clear (up to His saying: ) 'And none receive admonition except men of understanding.' Then he said: 'O 'Aishah, if you see those who dispute concerning it (the Qur'an), they are those whom Allah has referred to here, so beware of them.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 47)"
"77","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not acquire knowledge in order to boast before the scholars, or to argue with t"
"78","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:“Whoever acquires knowledge by which the pleasure of Allah can be attained, but he acquires it only for some worldly benefit, then on the Day of Resurrection he will not even smell the fragrance of Paradise.”This narration is also transmitted with another chain of narration."""
"79","Do not sit with those who believe in free will and do not address them before they address you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4720)"
"80","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “I fear most for you regarding this: you will argue with a smooth-tongued hypocrite.”"""
"81","The Prophet’s fear for his nation of the arguments of hypocrites."
"82","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saying: ""O Allah! I ask You for beneficial knowledge, and I seek refuge with You from knowledge that does not benefit."
"83","I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, from an action that is not elevated, from a heart that does not fear, and from a supplication that is not heard. (I seek refuge in You from all these)."",84,""If anyone pursues a path in search of knowledge, Allah will thereby make easy for him a path to paradise; and he who is made slow by his actions will not be speeded by his genealogy. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3643)"
"85","I went to Safwän bin 'Asal al-Murädi and he said: What brought you here?I said: I am seeking knowledge. He said: I heard the"",""Messenger of Allah say"",""“There is no one who goes out o f his house in order to seek knowledge except that the angels lower their wings in approval of his action.”"""",86,""Abu Waqid al-Laith reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque along wish tome people when there came to him three persons; two of them stepped forward to the direction of Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and one of them went away. The two stood by the side of Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and one of them found a space in his circle and he sat in that; and the other one sat behind him and the third one went away. When Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished his work, he said. Should I not inform you about these three persons? One of them sought refuge with Allah and Allah gave him refuge and the second one felt shy and Allah showed kindness to has shyness (and so he was accommodated in that meeting), and the last one reverted and Allah turned away His attention from him. (Using translation from Muslim 2176a)"
"87","narrates: He heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""Whoever comes to our mosque to acquire or teach knowledge of goodness, he is like one who strives in the way of Allah. And whoever comes for any other reason, his example is like that of a person who keeps an eye on something that does not belong to him."",88,""Kathir ibn Qays said: I was sitting with AbudDarda' in the mosque of Damascus. A man came to him and said: AbudDarda, I have come to you from the town of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a tradition that I have heard you relate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I have come for no other purpose. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: If anyone travels on a road in search of knowledge, Allah will cause him to travel on one of the roads of Paradise. The angels will lower their wings in their great pleasure with one who seeks knowledge, the inhabitants of the heavens and the Earth and the fish in the deep waters will ask forgiveness for the learned man. The superiority of the learned man over the devout is like that of the moon, on the night when it is full, over the rest of the stars. The learned are the heirs of the Prophets, and the Prophets leave neither dinar nor dirham, leaving only knowledge, and he who takes it takes an abundant portion. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3641)"",89,""I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, ""If Allah wants to do good to a person, He makes him comprehend the religion. I am just a distributor, but the grant is from Allah. (And remember) that this nation (true Muslims) will keep on following Allah's teachings strictly and they will not be harmed by any one going on a different path till Allah's order (Day of Judgment) is established."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 71)"",90,""“There is no (permissible) envy except in two cases: A man whom Allah has given wealth and caused him to dispose of it in a proper manner, and a man to whom Allah has given wisdom, and he acts in accordance with it and teaches it (to others).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4208)"",91,""I heard Abū al-Qāsim (the Prophet) ﷺ say, ""The best of you in Islam are those with the best character, if they have a good ˹religious˺ understanding."" (Using translation from Aḥmad 10066)"
"92","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""People are like mines of gold and silver (i.e., sources of good or evil). Those who were the best among them in the pre-Islamic era are also the best in Islam, provided they gain understanding of the religion."
"93","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""Among the things a man leaves behind after him, three things are the best: a righteous child who prays for him, a continuous charity whose reward reaches him, and knowledge through which benefit is obtained even after that person (has died)."" Imam Ibn Hibban (may Allah have mercy on him) says: ""There remain one hundred hadiths of this type, which we have mentioned in various types (i.e., chapters) of this book, because they are more appropriate to the subject matter of those chapters."",94,""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ Said: Forgive the people of good qualities their slips, but not faults to which prescribed penalties apply. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4375)"
"95","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever conceals knowledge, a bridle made of fire will be placed on him on the Day of Resurrection."
